  "query_preview": "../Thursday through Sunday/...\nA ridge of high pressure lasts over the Gulf and panhandle\nThursday into Friday, however a pattern change begins Friday into\nthe weekend with a return of a series of systems moving into the\narea. The first front will move in Friday from a low in the Bering\nSea, with the front primarily looking to push into the northern\nGulf coast Friday into Saturday morning, as the strong high\npressure looks to keep the front further westward with lower\nchances of pushing into the rest of the panhandle until Saturday.\nThe timing of this still looks to remain uncertain, largely\ndependent on how quickly the high pressure begins to break down\nwith this strong low pushing eastward. It seems that more of the\nmodel guidance is keeping the front further west, slowing down the\nonset of precipitation. Alongside the uncertainty of timing, \ndepending on when the front begins to push in will also affect \nthe precipitation type expected; if the front moves in overnight \ninto early Saturday morning, many locations across the northern\npanhandle may see rain with snow mixing in with the cold airmass \nin place and below freezing surface temperatures from overnight.\nHowever, if it moves in during the day Saturday and is delayed\nfurther on the timing, it is likely to begin as rain and stay\npredominantly rain, with the warmer air pushing into the area. \n\nThis more active pattern will continue through the weekend as a\nseries of lows move into the Gulf from the south around this main\nparent low as it moves eastward towards the AK Peninsula by \nSunday.",
